# Declaration kinds collected by the BY-VALUE checker spine and NOT by the
# *mut transcription that the default engine (Madaros) actually runs.
#
# Each line is a language feature that may be INERT on the default engine.
# "May be", not "is": some of these are plausibly handled by a later pass
# rather than by the collect pass, and this ledger does not claim to have
# checked each one. What it does claim is that nobody has checked, and that
# is exactly the state that let `algebra` and `unit` sit dead for months.
#
# THE RULE: this list may SHRINK. It may not grow. A new divergence fails
# scripts/ci/checker_spine_parity_gate.sh. Removing a line means either the
# arm was wired into checker_collect_item_inplace, or someone established
# where it is handled instead and recorded that in the commit.
#
# Measured 2026-09-09 against self-hosted/check/check.sio:
#   by-value collect_item          28 ItemKind arms
#   checker_collect_item_inplace   10 ItemKind arms
#
# Two entries were on this list until this commit and are not any more:
#   ItemAlgebra  wired 2026-09-01, after `algebra {}` was found inert
#   ItemUnit     wired 2026-09-09, after units of measure were found inert
#                (11 of 14 unit fixtures failed on Madaros, 14 of 14 passed
#                on lean_single)
#
# ItemOntology is the confirmed-broken one, and an attempt to wire it on
# 2026-09-09 was REVERTED. What that attempt measured is the useful part:
#
#   Wiring the STRUCTURAL layer alone -- class registration, superclasses,
#   property refinements, disjointness, closure, and binding class names into
#   the type environment -- took the ontology fixtures from 40 of 42 passing
#   to 11, with a mix of E152 "cannot prove ontology subsumption" and
#   SIGSEGV.
#
#   The E152s explain the whole picture. ontology_inference_query_subclass
#   reads the KERNEL structures, which only ontology_inference_collect_kernel
#   populates. Wire the class table without the kernel and every subsumption
#   query answers false, so `fn accept(d: Drug)` rejects a Rapamycin that is
#   declared its subclass.
#
#   And it explains why those 40 fixtures were green to begin with: with
#   ItemOntology uncollected, ontology_id was never set on any type, so every
#   ontology boundary check early-returned and passed. THE SUBSYSTEM WAS
#   INERT AND THE TESTS WERE PASSING BECAUSE OF IT. Turning half of it on is
#   worse than leaving it off, because the checks then fire against an empty
#   kernel.
#
#   Reaching the kernel through a by-value bridge is not an option either:
#   the Checker is ~8 MB and copying it onto the stack segfaults regardless of
#   call depth. That was tried in the same attempt and produced SIGSEGV on 40
#   of the 42 fixtures.
#
# SO: ItemOntology is all-or-nothing. Closing it means transcribing the axiom
# layer too -- ontology_inference_collect_kernel, its four collectors, and the
# two validation passes, about 270 lines -- and landing the whole thing at
# once. The arithmetic-level rule that layer would then enable is drafted in
# scratchpad/layer3_ontology_arithmetic.sio.txt.

ItemAcquisitionPolicy
ItemAlternativeFrontier
ItemAlternativePolicy
ItemAudit
ItemCausalGraph
ItemClaim
ItemDecisionPolicy
ItemDeferralPolicy
ItemEffect
ItemMonitoringPolicy
ItemOntology
ItemRecoursePolicy
ItemSession
ItemStudy
ItemTrait
ItemTransitionPolicy
ItemTransitionProtocol
ItemValidation
